Save93 / AE 1.6.1170 / SSE Display Tweaks 0.5.16 / gameplay 42 FPS cap
Cross-scene diagnosis. The equipment group is the four disabled trials of the previous gameplay A/B. The cell group is a separate run from the same Save93 with stock scheduling and four COC transitions between Whiterun exterior and the Bannered Mare.
Initial cell pilot aborted in trial 2 when response requests piled up in the SKSE task queue during loading. That pilot is excluded below. The revised benchmark waits for observed arrival and UI-ready, then one second before dispatching 32 response probes over 8 seconds. This is a post-load sample; actual render rate is measured separately.
Cell roots are the traced cell/load/location event types first queued from the travel request until response probing begins. The tail is the latest completed root in that group. Open counts do not include work that never entered a root during the capture. Native waits are profiler Q-P on that stack, with a 1 ms floor for listing chains. Adjacent native calls may have intervening script bytecode.
Only the render periods validated against engine counters are reported. The final two seconds are shown separately because the 42 FPS cap does not guarantee the game reaches it during streaming.
Exact pair intersections apply only to the measured last handlers. Cell travel is not a combat benchmark. No continuation optimization was activated.

